    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Publish the current designer draft as a standard local template package.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT REQUIRED Source draft reference, e.g. local://designer-draft.\r\n          --slot TEXT         Replaceable material selection: all, or seg_id=<id>;seg_id=<id>.\r\n                              Omit to preserve every source material as fixed.\r\n          --dir TEXT          Optional parent directory for the isolated external designer\r\n                              draft workspace.\r\n          --source-mode TEXT  Publisher source: session (default) or external_designer_draft.\r\n          --source-json TEXT  Required with --source-mode external_designer_draft: absolute\r\n                              path to the decrypted source draft JSON.\r\n          --source-root TEXT  Optional complete external designer draft root used to stage\r\n                              relative fixed resources.\r\n          --selection-start-ms INT \r\n                              Optional external designer draft highlight start in milliseconds.\r\n          --selection-duration-ms INT \r\n                              Optional external designer draft highlight duration in\r\n                              milliseconds.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Publish a designer draft with two replaceable video slots\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template publish --ref local://designer-draft \\\r\n      --dir /tmp/lyra-template-publisher \\\r\n      --source-mode external_designer_draft \\\r\n      --source-json /abs/path/template.decrypted.json \\\r\n      --source-root /abs/path/designer-draft \\\r\n      --selection-start-ms 12000 --selection-duration-ms 8000 \\\r\n      --slot 'seg_id=<video-segment-1>;seg_id=<video-segment-2>'\r\n\r\nThe command uses the native template publisher and returns a local template.zip. Use that zip with `lyra-cli draft template add --resource local:///.../template.zip`.\r\nOnly declared slots are mutable; fixed effects, stickers, filters, audio and fonts remain native template dependencies.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Publish the current designer draft as a standard local template package.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT REQUIRED Source draft reference, e.g. local://designer-draft.\r\n          --slot TEXT         Replaceable material selection: all, or seg_id=<id>;seg_id=<id>.\r\n                              Omit to preserve every source material as fixed.\r\n          --dir TEXT          Optional parent directory for the isolated external designer\r\n                              draft workspace.\r\n          --source-mode TEXT  Publisher source: session (default) or external_designer_draft.\r\n          --source-json TEXT  Required with --source-mode external_designer_draft: absolute\r\n                              path to the decrypted source draft JSON.\r\n          --source-root TEXT  Optional complete external designer draft root used to stage\r\n                              relative fixed resources.\r\n          --selection-start-ms INT \r\n                              Optional external designer draft highlight start in milliseconds.\r\n          --selection-duration-ms INT \r\n                              Optional external designer draft highlight duration in\r\n                              milliseconds.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Publish a designer draft with two replaceable video slots\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft template publish --ref local://designer-draft \\\r\n      --dir /tmp/lyra-template-publisher \\\r\n      --source-mode external_designer_draft \\\r\n      --source-json /abs/path/template.decrypted.json \\\r\n      --source-root /abs/path/designer-draft \\\r\n      --selection-start-ms 12000 --selection-duration-ms 8000 \\\r\n      --slot 'seg_id=<video-segment-1>;seg_id=<video-segment-2>'\r\n\r\nThe command uses the native template publisher and returns a local template.zip. Use that zip with `lyra-cli draft template add --resource local:///.../template.zip`.\r\nOnly declared slots are mutable; fixed effects, stickers, filters, audio and fonts remain native template dependencies.\r\n",
